# Busy and free in Russian: я за́нят
subtitle: "Say you're busy, ready, right or ill in Russian: за́нят and занята́, гото́в, прав, бо́лен and больна́, with no word for am and the endings of был, была́."
tags: ["russian","short adjectives","занят","russian grammar","готов"]
teaches: ["grammar/short-adjectives"]
thumb: "band \"I busy. Perfectly correct.\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Holidays in Russian: с Но́вым го́дом!","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/89-russian-holidays.cast"}

## Busy and free in Russian: я за́нят
level: basic

